//! English adjectives, built on 3 principal parts: each cell belongs to the system of
//! one part and is inflected from that part's form. A word's parts are what
//! you give, else what the part's own grammar gives for its lemma (which
//! lists the dictionary's parts it doesn't predict).
//!
//! Generated by flexion-train from Wiktionary; don't edit by hand.

